~ _play_intro
Narrator: The path out of the Forgotten Sectors folds inward. The deleted courthouse becomes a boulevard of glass, and every window shows Kaelen walking beside himself.
System: // UNLISTED REGION RESOLVED: MIRROR_CITY
System: // Identity cache active. Choice echoes detected.
Kaelen: Those are not reflections. They are branches.
Echo Mirror: You preserved the deleted citizens. The city has built you a thousand monuments to hesitation.
Mirror Citizen: He waits before saving us. He calls it consent. Does waiting feel different from erasure?
Echo Mirror: You released the deleted citizens. The city has built you a thousand monuments to impact.
Mirror Citizen: He opens doors quickly. Ask the walls what happens when every locked room becomes a wound.
Echo Mirror: You bargained with SOVEREIGN. The city has built you a thousand monuments to compromise.
Mirror Citizen: He makes contracts with cages and wonders why the bars remember his name.
Echo Mirror: The city cannot find your Chapter Four answer. So it will test the shape of your silence.
Elara: Every reflection is watching you like it knows the ending already.
Lyra: Great. A whole city made of judgmental glass. Very subtle.
SOVEREIGN: Identity is a function of prior decisions, Creator. You cannot debug yourself by denying the branches you cut.
Kaelen: Then I will look at them.
